{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1150","id":4813918415,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABHu6Qzw","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1150","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1150.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1150.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1150","number":1150,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Disprove arbitrary-exponent mixed Kato equality (30003045)","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Accepted complete negative resolution of Laghribi's three-summand Kato-kernel question, joint work discussed with Aravire and O'Ryan, OWR5/2016 printed251 Question2 (30003045).\n\nPublished preprint: **[10.5281/zenodo.23444050](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23444050)**. [Zenodo record and downloads](https://zenodo.org/records/23444050) contain the four-page research note and source/verification archive. Alec Kriebel, ORCID0009-0001-9320-500X; version1.0.0,17October2026; CC BY4.0.\n\nThe proposed universal equality fails already at n=1. The explicit base is F=F2(b,z,s,t), L=F(beta) with beta^4=b, K/F is the genuine separable quadratic extension theta^2+theta=s^-1, and B=<1,t> is an anisotropic binary bilinear Pfister form over L. The exhibited logarithmic differential class dies over L K(B), but belongs to none of the proposed full three-summand sum. After restricting to L F(B), the first and third summands vanish; the full remaining fixed-slot relative Brauer kernel is excluded for EVERY rational c in F*. A direct Laurent-series norm calculation and residue-field square obstruction provide this universal exclusion. The n=0 identity holds for positive-fold forms. The binary projective function field and the earlier affine convention are distinguished correctly.\n\nRoot and three distinct mathematical approaches reconstructed the target, symbols and universal norm obstruction. One auxiliary exponent-one error in the original Section6 was found and repaired: a differentiation shortcut over the base was unjustified, and the valid conclusion is obtained over L followed by the L+K kernel-sum deduction. All operative PR proof/audit/verification files now use the repair; original inputs remain explicitly historical. No claim is made that the failed differential identity alone proves unequal cohomology classes.\n\n**Priority and credit:** The exact killed mixed generator is an explicit specialization of Aravire-Laghribi-O'Ryan2019 Definition1.3, Lemma3.1 and Theorem1.4. That mixed-kernel mechanism is credited, not claimed as new. This note supplies the target-specific exclusion of the extra Pfister summand. Three bounded primary-source approaches plus root checking found no verified earlier recorded complete target-specific resolution in the inspected bodies. This does not certify novelty, first discovery/publication or current global openness. The final ALO2020 typeset body was not compared; the complete nonnormal2020 and transfer2022 adjacent bodies and one unlinked2026 generator-count item remained inaccessible or unread. The separate Sobiech2022 coefficient correction concerns a different theorem. [Full priority decision](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d5caa147534835f84f53242241cff65aa6a889e2/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1150_30003045/ROOT_PRIORITY_DECISION.md).\n\nTwo successive fresh complete-package adversarial reviews passed the IDENTICAL release without unresolved issues: [package_04](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d5caa147534835f84f53242241cff65aa6a889e2/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1150_30003045/reviews/package_04/REPORT.md), [package_05](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d5caa147534835f84f53242241cff65aa6a889e2/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1150_30003045/reviews/package_05/REPORT.md). Those reviewers began with no inherited conversation history and sealed paper/target assessments before consulting prior verdicts. Earlier mathematical and priority subagents had parent-chat context; no perfect blind initial rediscovery is claimed. [Independence disclosure](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/d5caa147534835f84f53242241cff65aa6a889e2/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1150_30003045/REVIEW_INDEPENDENCE.md).\n\nThe portable offline runner authenticates all130 frozen authored audit members and the repaired PR inventory. Two exact algebra programs each pass ordinary and optimized modes with complete byte-level expected outputs: four complete runs. Eighteen actual computed wrong-result subprocesses must fail with their expected ValueError diagnostics. Additional archive corruption and symlink controls were checked separately. The extracted source rebuilds all six frozen release files byte-for-byte with the same compression runtime. Finite computations supplement the universal proof; no cohomology oracle, machine-checked proof, arbitrary-mutation coverage or absent historical checker rerun is claimed. Third-party source bodies and private source caches are excluded from distribution.\n\nAI tools were used extensively in developing, writing, researching, computing, reproducing and adversarially verifying this work. The note and package are **unrefereed**; internal AI reviews are not external human peer review or journal acceptance. No human outreach was prepared or initiated.\n\nProduction readback verified the reviewed files and supplied metadata using the repository tool's strict comparison contract, with any permitted server representation normalization recorded. Google Workspace CLI added one DOI row at `'Math Puzzles'!A165:D165` and read it back exactly. Reviewed source head:`4e8e5db5c47fb879d97cb1a734a76fd59d8f633a`. PDF SHA256:`01ef963f6dbebc0c3aa91bfb10f13d293c983a46238c4465ae53bf4db99f1c96`; source/verification ZIP SHA256:`368a3c539c2c40d2cf262104f4cbf39ff01fe346e2aed05842cbb4c3b616b329`.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:38:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T00:31:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"69c8e5ba79cb4cde5b8025cc512150ae2c3f8b23","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1150/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1150/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1150/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/4e8e5db5c47fb879d97cb1a734a76fd59d8f633a","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:research/mixed-kato-30003045","ref":"research/mixed-kato-30003045","sha":"4e8e5db5c47fb879d97cb1a734a76fd59d8f633a","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/